3. Mechanical layout on the pole (top → bottom)





Top: 50 W panel, tilted ~15–25° toward the equator (India: face south).



Upper canopy: 12 V LED lamps facing both carriageways; optional air-purifier housing with weather cover and insect mesh.



Side of shaft (1–1.5 m above median, in vehicle wake): Savonius rotor. Keep blades outside the vehicle envelope and behind crash barrier rules for a real highway; this prototype is for a lab/campus road.



Locked IP65 box at chest height: battery, 30 A controller, buck/boost, ESP32, relays, fuses.



Ventilation: LiFePO4 is safer than lead‑acid but still needs airflow and no standing water.



