5. Build order (safety)





Mount pole, panel, turbine, and IP65 box. No electrical connections yet.



Fit fuses holders empty.



Wire battery negative as the common ground star.



Connect battery to the 30 A controller BAT+/BAT− first. Set battery type to LiFePO4 if the menu has it (otherwise use a controller that supports LFP).



Confirm controller shows ~12.8–13.4 V.



Connect solar PV+/PV− last. Cover the panel until the connector is seated.



Set XL6009 on a bench supply to 14.4 V output before attaching the turbine. Then add the Schottky diode toward battery +.



Set LM2596S output to 5.00 V with a multimeter before plugging in the ESP32.



Wire sensors and relays on the 5 V / 3.3 V side.



Insert fuses, one at a time, starting with the 5 A electronics fuse.



Flash ESP32 firmware (same logic as Wokwi wokwi/sketch.ino).



Only then connect lamps and (if used) inverter + purifier.



6. Wind turbine electrical note

Most small Savonius kits use a DC generator or a 3-phase hub + rectifier.





If AC 3-phase: use the kit bridge rectifier, then XL6009.



If already DC: diode → XL6009 → battery.



Never feed raw turbine voltage into the ESP32.



A highway-wake Savonius on a short pole often produces only a few watts. Treat solar as the main source for the demo.



